title: Falcon/XG "PDF Viewer" Chrome Extension Artifacts Created on Disk
id: 450e76ca-d012-46e3-8801-5c2d4aa15a2c
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects file creation inside the profile directory of the Chrome extension
    that ships with the Falcon (XG / Xiang Ge) browser C2 framework. The
    framework injects JavaScript into webmail portals and government web
    applications and keeps its implant inside the victim's browser tab, and it
    installs a companion extension posing as "PDF Viewer" with ID
    mbidcmlcbgbphpoacojjbmfpohcimjji that requests roughly 40 permissions for
    credential, cookie, history, clipboard and network access. The same
    intrusion drops the Antino Rust backdoor, whose command and control rides
    Microsoft Graph against Outlook and OneDrive. The extension ID is a fixed
    artifact reported by Unit 42, so a match is a direct hit rather than a
    behavioral guess. The rule ships without a product qualifier so browser
    extension directories on any endpoint telemetry source can match.
references:
    - https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/falcon-c2-browser-compromise/
    - https://blog.talosintelligence.com/china-nexus-uat-11587-targets-government-and-policy-organizations-across-asia-with-antino-backdoor/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/13
tags:
    - attack.t1176
    - attack.t1185
logsource:
    category: file_event
detection:
    selection_extension_id:
        TargetFilename|contains: 'mbidcmlcbgbphpoacojjbmfpohcimjji'
    condition: selection_extension_id
falsepositives:
    - Malware analysts or threat-intel tooling staging artifacts of the reported extension ID in an isolated profile or sandbox
    - Enterprise browsers syncing an archived extension directory whose folder name carries the same identifier
level: high
